1
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:18,000
Excuse me. Is this seat taken?

2
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,200
No, it's not taken.

3
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,300
Oh, thank you.

4
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:21,682
Oh, let me help you with this.

5
00:00:21,682 --> 00:00:27,282
Oh, thank you.

6
00:00:27,282 --> 00:00:28,300
Do you want to sit by the window?

7
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,700
No, no, no. I like the aisle seat better.

8
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:38,175
Please, you sit by the window.

9
00:00:38,175 --> 00:00:39,600
My name is Stewart... Malcolm Stewart.

10
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:40,400
Pleased to meet you.

11
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:47,400
I'm Elsa Tobin. How do you do?

12
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:49,200
Do you live in New York?

13
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:51,200
No, no. I'm from Florida.

14
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:56,200
I am, too. But didn't you just get on?

15
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:58,165
No, no. I just changed my seat.

16
00:00:58,165 --> 00:00:59,800
A man next to me was smoking,

17
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:04,600
and smoke really bothers me.

18
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:06,300
Where are you from in Florida?

19
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:08,698
Titusville. It's near Orlando.

20
00:01:08,698 --> 00:01:10,800
Small world. I'm from Titusville, too.

21
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:14,100
Really? What part?

22
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:16,200
My husband and I live near Spaceport.

23
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:18,642
I know that area.

24
00:01:18,642 --> 00:01:23,000
My house is only a few miles from Spaceport.

25
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:23,960
Do you still live there?

26
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:25,900
Oh yes, yes. My husband's there now.

27
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:31,400
He couldn't take time off to come to New York with me.

28
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:33,000
Do you still live there?

29
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,307
No. I sold the house and the furniture,

30
00:01:38,307 --> 00:01:42,000
put a few personal things in an old trunk,

31
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:43,900
and shipped it to my children in New York.

32
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:46,600
That's my destination.

33
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,712
Are you married?

34
00:01:47,712 --> 00:01:51,300
My wife died four years ago.

35
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:54,200
She was a wonderful woman. A real friend.

36
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:59,500
I'm sorry. Really, I'm sorry.

37
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:01,708
Lots of wonderful memories.

38
00:02:01,708 --> 00:02:03,400
We were married almost fifty years.

39
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,923
Well, forty-seven, to be exact.

40
00:02:05,923 --> 00:02:08,600
John and I celebrate our fortieth anniversary next month.

41
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:13,800
Oh, congratulations! That's nice.

42
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,000
What does John do?

43
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,900
He's an aerospace engineer

44
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:19,646
and works for Orlando Aircraft Corporation.

45
00:02:19,646 --> 00:02:24,200
He started with them almost forty years ago.

46
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:25,571
What do you do?

47
00:02:25,571 --> 00:02:29,600
I just retired. Had my own company.

48
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:35,300
A construction company. Roads, bridges, big stuff.

49
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:42,300
But I just sold it and retired.

50
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:46,500
Excuse me, ma'am. Ticket, please.

51
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:50,033
Would you kindly hold these keys, please?

52
00:02:50,033 --> 00:02:52,205
I have a ticket, I know.

53
00:02:52,205 --> 00:02:53,600
I was in the smoking section.

54
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:56,625
It's OK, lady. Take your time.

55
00:02:56,625 --> 00:02:58,900
I'm sure it's in your purse, Mrs.Tobin.

56
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:03,800
Oh, here it is.

57
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,600
And here are your keys.

58
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:11,100
Thank you.

59
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:12,973
Do you have family in New York?

60
00:03:12,973 --> 00:03:17,872
No, no. But I do have very close friends in New York City.

61
00:03:17,872 --> 00:03:21,000
We like to go to the theater together.

62
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,500
You said you have family in New York.

63
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:23,400
Yes, indeed.

64
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:27,285
A son and his wife and their three children-

65
00:03:27,285 --> 00:03:28,600
my grandchildren.

66
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:29,397
You must be excited.

67
00:03:29,397 --> 00:03:33,100
I can't wait, to see them!

68
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:34,200
Are you going to live with them?

69
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:35,066
Yes.

70
00:03:35,066 --> 00:03:36,400
Permanently?

71
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:40,264
Well... they want me to,

72
00:03:40,264 --> 00:03:42,410
but it's too early to know for sure.

73
00:03:42,410 --> 00:03:44,719
I'm pretty independent.

74
00:03:44,719 --> 00:03:48,900
I tried to teach my kids the importance of independence,

75
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:53,700
but I'm not sure I want to be alone.

76
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:58,100
Some people don't mind being alone. I do.

77
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:01,340
I understand. But tell me.

78
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:03,900
Why did you stop working?

79
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:11,284
I retired because... I wanted to be with my family.

80
00:04:11,284 --> 00:04:14,284
I didn't want to be alone anymore!
